      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Supporters argue that vouchers empower parents to choose the best education for their children regardless of the school they are zoned for, which can improve academic outcomes and increase competition among schools. Conversely, opponents contend that vouchers divert public funds away from underfunded public schools, exacerbate inequality, and undermine the public school system that would otherwise benefit from those same taxpayer dollars. Because of these conflicting views, the debate ultimately centers on whether individual choice is more valuable than a blanket commitment to public education for all students.",
