      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The evidence on vouchers is mixed and often depends heavily on the specific local implementation and outcome measures used by researchers. While some studies show test score improvements in low-income areas, others indicate increased segregation and potential financial burdens on the public system. The debate is indeed complex and doesn't boil down solely to political fear; it involves legitimate economic and social trade-offs that manifest differently across communities.",
      "source": "target",
